@attribute [Route($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_NavGroup}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Usage}")]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_NavGroup @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Usage</PageTitle>

<h1>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_NavGroup @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Usage</h1>

<p>
    Practical examples showing the Nav Group component configured with various parameters.
</p>
<p>
    The following example is the NavGroup being used inside a HTML <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">nav</span> element but as there is no width set its taking all of the available width. 
    I have given both the nested NavSection components and the single NavGroupLink component icons and set the initial <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Expanded</span> parameter
    to true.
</p>
<nav aria-label="navigation example">
    <NavGroup>
        <NavSection SvgIcon="--svg-component-icon" Title="Components" Expanded="true">
            <NavSection SvgIcon="--svg-open-book-icon" Title="Documentation" Expanded="true">
                    <NavGroupLink SvgIcon="--svg-article-icon" Href="" LinkText="Fake article" VisuallyHiddenPrefix="Documentation" TargetType="TargetType.Self" />
            </NavSection>
        </NavSection>
    </NavGroup>
</nav>
<ThemeBorderTool Title="Applicable theme border tools" ThemeToolHeadingLevel="ThemeToolHeadingLevel.H2">
    <BorderGroups>
        <BorderGroup Title="Menu borders">
            <BorderRadius LabelText="Trigger, panel radius" ResetText="Reset trigger, panel radius" MaxRangeValue="@GlobalValues.Radius_Menu_Trigger_Panel_Max_Range_Value"
                          CssProperties="@([new(CoreCssVariables.Group_Menu_Radius_Panel), new(CoreCssVariables.Group_Menu_Radius_Header), new(CoreCssVariables.Group_Menu_Radius_Content)])" />
            <BorderRadius LabelText="Menu item radius" ResetText="Reset menu item radius" MaxRangeValue="@GlobalValues.Radius_Menu_Item_Max_Range_Value" CssProperties="@([new(CoreCssVariables.Group_Menu_Radius_item)])" />
        </BorderGroup>
    </BorderGroups>
</ThemeBorderTool>
<h2>
    Code from the example
</h2>
<CodeBox CodeBlock="@NavGroupSnippets.Usage_example" AriaLabel="Nav group code example" />
<p>
    As the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Href</span> parameter has be set to the an empty string the default of <b>"missing-href"</b> will be used, leading to a page not found if activated.
</p>
<p>
    Although the left hand navigation on this site uses multiple NavGroup components with headings, I could have used a single NavGroup with NavSection components 
    in place of the headings.
</p>
<p>
    <strong>Note: </strong>The NavGroup component is designed to be used on an interactive page.
</p>
<div class="flex-content justify-content-between">
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Button_Class @GlobalValues.Link_Button_Left_Arrow_Modifier" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_NavGroup}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Api}")">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_NavGroup - @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Api</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </a>
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Button_Class @GlobalValues.Link_Button_Right_Arrow_Modifier" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Pager}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Overview}")">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Pager - @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Overview</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </a>
</div>
